1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,141
Priya's renewals do not fail because she is careless.

2
00:00:03,141 --> 00:00:07,458
They slip because a hundred small tasks compete for the same Tuesday, and a follow

3
00:00:07,458 --> 00:00:10,196
up due in eight days loses to whatever is due today.

4
00:00:10,196 --> 00:00:14,461
This agent's entire job is noticing the eight-day ones before they become today's

5
00:00:14,461 --> 00:00:18,041
problem, and handing you a draft instead of a reason to feel behind.

6
00:00:18,041 --> 00:00:19,936
Why a draft, rather than a reminder?

7
00:00:19,936 --> 00:00:23,464
Because a reminder adds a task to your day and a draft removes one.

8
00:00:23,464 --> 00:00:27,729
"Chase Brightwell" on a to-do list still costs you the finding, the phrasing, the

9
00:00:27,729 --> 00:00:31,151
polite-but-firm calibration, at the exact moment you are busiest.

10
00:00:31,151 --> 00:00:33,784
A draft sitting ready costs you a read and a send.

11
00:00:33,784 --> 00:00:37,943
The difference sounds small and compounds enormously: the chase that takes four

12
00:00:37,943 --> 00:00:42,261
seconds happens, every time, and the chase that takes four minutes is the one that

13
00:00:42,261 --> 00:00:42,576
slips.

14
00:00:42,576 --> 00:00:44,998
This agent does not make you more disciplined.

15
00:00:44,998 --> 00:00:48,579
It makes the disciplined action nearly free, which works far better.

16
00:00:49,129 --> 00:00:53,714
Read the action line again, because it is written differently from the first three

17
00:00:53,714 --> 00:00:55,280
job descriptions on purpose.

18
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:59,977
It does not say "mostly draft" or "draft unless." It says draft only, full stop, and

19
00:00:59,977 --> 00:01:04,507
the build in this section is going to prove that sentence is true in your wiring,

20
00:01:04,507 --> 00:01:05,513
not just on paper.

21
00:01:05,513 --> 00:01:08,253
Write your own version of it before you open n8n.

22
00:01:08,253 --> 00:01:11,273
Two other lines have grown teeth since the last build.

23
00:01:11,273 --> 00:01:15,691
The scope line says this agent writes drafts into a real mailbox, and that is a

24
00:01:15,691 --> 00:01:20,053
threshold worth saying out loud: for the first time in this course, an agent's

25
00:01:20,053 --> 00:01:24,470
output will live inside one of your actual work systems, wearing your account's

26
00:01:24,470 --> 00:01:24,750
name.

27
00:01:24,750 --> 00:01:29,280
That is exactly why the trial is the strictest yet, two weeks, every single draft

28
00:01:29,280 --> 00:01:31,349
read before anything is sent by hand.

29
00:01:31,349 --> 00:01:36,046
And the ceiling bans the premium amount from every draft, which is not squeamishness

30
00:01:36,046 --> 00:01:36,717
about money.

31
00:01:36,717 --> 00:01:41,135
A chase email gets forwarded, and a number that was fine between Priya and Ravi

32
00:01:41,135 --> 00:01:45,049
reads very differently when it lands in front of his finance director.

33
00:01:45,049 --> 00:01:49,691
Money figures belong in conversations a person chose to have, not in nudges a robot

34
00:01:49,691 --> 00:01:50,138
drafted.

35
00:01:50,138 --> 00:01:53,885
The polite chase works without the number, so the number stays out.

36
00:01:54,435 --> 00:01:57,106
The house-framing image is doing precise work.

37
00:01:57,106 --> 00:02:01,636
A lock added while framing sits square in the door and nobody ever debates it.

38
00:02:01,636 --> 00:02:06,339
A lock bolted on after a break-in arrives as a patch, under stress, argued about,

39
00:02:06,339 --> 00:02:07,617
and trusted by nobody.

40
00:02:07,617 --> 00:02:12,321
Constraints on agents age exactly the same way: draft-only built in on day one is

41
00:02:12,321 --> 00:02:17,141
simply what this agent is, invisible and unresented, while draft-only imposed after

42
00:02:17,141 --> 00:02:20,741
an incident reads as a demotion someone will eventually relax.

43
00:02:20,741 --> 00:02:25,387
Section 8's near miss shows the difference from the inside, on this exact agent.

44
00:02:25,387 --> 00:02:29,859
Next lecture starts the build, and the first piece is deciding which renewals

45
00:02:29,859 --> 00:02:34,563
actually deserve a chase this week, using the same pipeline sheet Agent 3 already

46
00:02:34,563 --> 00:02:35,666
taught you to read.
